<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tiridates III of Armenia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 330</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a> · Also known as Tiridates the Great</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tiridates III was Arsacid king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a> from the late 3rd century until about 330, restored with Roman support after a period of Sasanian rule. Converted by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gregory-the-illuminator">Gregory the Illuminator</a>, he made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> the state religion of Armenia in about 301, traditionally the first kingdom to do so, and backed the founding of the cathedral of Etchmiadzin.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tiridates-iii-of-armenia.jpg" alt="Tiridates III of Armenia" width="320" height="460" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gaidzakian, Ohan, 1837-1914 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tiridates_III_illustration.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
